From 7dd1097f3bdce37fbd500b34c25643173f0cf24a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:27:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(od-sevev): never leave the ticker strip empty between
 headlines (D19)

The pager rolled an empty page node in whenever a headline ended with
nothing queued, and in the first minute nothing refills it (ambient lines
wait for C1), so the row showed the plate, Dubi and the date over a blank
clip. A one-page headline now holds until the next one rolls in (up to
15 s); a multi-page headline, an FTUE line or a spent hold roll to the
standing line TICKER_IDLE, which is also the row before its first
headline. New unit test samples every frame; mobile_web checks the strip
at card 1, bought and C1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJWVH11egMQ4r4GfyoMb4p
