From 8b03f3575b22ad707210cea0c2d235572e2bd971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(od-sevev): rule the card pane, complete the tab bar,
 fade the teasers, anchor the chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D20: the white field reads as a ruled margin, not a gap: a flag-blue
1-art rule on each canvas edge, 3 art of white, then the card (the
4-art gutter rule holds). The scroll thumb rides the left rule and hides
when idle.
D21: the tab bar always shows four slots. The plate comes from the kit's
divider-free column, the engine draws one divider per slot boundary,
and an unrevealed slot draws its icon as a quiet silhouette with the
kit padlock where the label goes (not a target).
B9: the first teaser carries a one-line hint ("עוד מקורות ייפתחו"); the
rest are wordless slips fading down, never under 0.2, so the pane keeps
no empty band.
B11: a short chat thread starts under the header with a day chip
("היום") instead of sitting at the bottom of an empty blue field, and
the player's reply is headed by the round's leader's name so it reads
as a message row, not a loose chip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJWVH11egMQ4r4GfyoMb4p
